SURVIVOR b-sample-full-when-k-max: a draw below K = 1,000,000 is always true (uniform(1e6) is at most 999,999), so the sample is every fit row either way, in the same order: the shortcut only saves the draws
SURVIVOR b-sample-rounding: K differs only when subsample * 1e6 has a fractional part of 0.5 or more; the values of the suite (0.5, 0.8, 0.25, 0.999999) have none, and IEEE products like 0.8 * 1e6 = 800000.0000000001 truncate to the same K
SURVIVOR b-validation-loss-mean-over-m: a constant factor of every round's loss does not change which round is best, nor the rule 'no improvement': the stopping round is the same (the loss itself is not stored)
SURVIVOR b-fit-non-finite-check-removed: not reachable: a regression target is bounded by 1e100 and n by 2^20, so no score or sum overflows (docs/models-boost.md section 3.3); the check defends a bound that someone might widen
