SURVIVOR b-read-depth-of-a-tree: NO REASON GIVEN
SURVIVOR b-read-pending-children: the same argument as the tree library's reader (docs/models-tree.md section 7): a pending right child can never be popped by a node of the tree, and a pushed right child at the end belongs to a last node that is internal, which has its left child missing: every one-field edit that leaves a child pending also breaks the offsets or the left-is-next rule first
SURVIVOR b-adapter-threads-not-passed: an equivalent mutant by design: no thread count changes a byte of the model (the property GB2 asserts, and the binning is the only threaded part), so a fit that ignores the flag writes the same file
SURVIVOR b-adapter-class-of-one-half: a probability of exactly 0.5 needs a score whose sigmoid rounds to one half: |score| below 1e-16, a sum of leaf values that cancel to the last bit: the generated rows never reach it (the same tie as the tree's `wt-class-of-a-tie`)
SURVIVOR b-adapter-proba-of-a-regression: a second line of defence: predict --proba on a regression is args.conflict before the adapter is called and eval asks for a probability only of a classification
